llcv (2.1.4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Follow the Windows LLCV 2.1.4 update.
  * F2 and Settings in the menu always open the default page: Video, or
    Audio in audio-only mode. Recording options stay on the Recording tab.
  * Fix possible loss of the last video and audio packets when capture
    delivery overlaps the end of a recording.
  * Invalid numbers in settings.ini (trailing characters or values out of
    the int range) fall back to the defaults.
  * The drift-correction resampler sums its normalization once per frame,
    with unchanged output.

 -- Meohong <busimh001@gmail.com>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900

llcv (2.1.3.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Fix the .deb packages of 2.1.3, which could not be installed on Ubuntu
    24.04 and 26.04, Debian 12 and 13 or Raspberry Pi OS 64-bit (trixie):
    they depended on the FFmpeg libraries of the release they were built
    on. The packages now contain a minimal FFmpeg 7.1.1 (AAC, x264, NVENC,
    VA-API and the MP4 muxer) linked statically, so one package per
    architecture works on every supported release again. Only libva is
    used from the system.
  * In the .deb packages, CPU recording is H.264 (x264); HEVC and AV1 need
    NVENC or VA-API. The armhf package is built without x264, because the
    distribution's static x264 cannot be linked into a position-independent
    executable there, and without NVENC, which FFmpeg does not offer on
    32-bit ARM. Fedora and Arch keep using the system FFmpeg.

 -- Meohong <busimh001@gmail.com>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0900

llcv (2.1.3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Follow the Windows LLCV 2.1.0, 2.1.1, 2.1.2 and 2.1.3 updates.
  * MP4 recording (F9, Settings → Recording) through FFmpeg. NV12, YUY2,
    MJPEG and BGR24 SDR video with 16-bit stereo capture audio is saved as
    fragmented MP4 with H.264, HEVC or AV1 on NVENC, VA-API or CPU encoders
    (x264, x265, SVT-AV1). Quality (constant QP) or target bitrate, 1080p and
    60 fps limits by default, AAC 128/192 kbps, a recording volume separate
    from playback, pause/resume from the Alt menu and automatic splitting by
    duration or size. Encoder support is checked when the Recording page
    opens; unsupported combinations report an error instead of switching.
    Opening settings or quitting asks before stopping and saving a
    recording. HDR input is not recorded.
  * Playback mute (M) from the audio OSD, the audio-only view or the Audio
    menu. A translucent icon stays at the top right while the audio OSD is
    hidden. Recorded sound is not muted; the wheel and volume up/down unmute
    playback. Existing custom shortcuts are kept, and Recording and Mute get
    a free function key when F9 or M is already taken.
  * Allow unlisted FPS (Video): a direct 30 fps request when the driver does
    not list it, confirmed on Start without falling back to another rate.
  * Fullscreen video size (fit to screen or original size) and position
    (center, edges or corners) under Window.
  * Colorimetry is read again after streaming starts, so the final MJPEG
    color range and matrix apply.
  * The window position is no longer saved while the window is minimized.
  * More Windows features: HDR chroma placement override for P010, hardware
    HDR-to-SDR requests for AVerMedia UVC-extension and Elgato HD60 S+/X
    devices (with a udev rule for the Elgato HID interface), fullscreen
    start and F5 fullscreen when the capture matches the monitor, keep
    relative window size across monitors, double-click to reset a volume to
    100 %, mouse wheel per channel, orange boosted volume, a movable and
    aspect-locked audio-only view that follows Borderless window, Open last
    recording, and Cancel in settings opened during playback.
  * Recording keeps up to about 0.75 s of frames so CPU encoders no longer
    drop frames at keyframes.

 -- Meohong <busimh001@gmail.com>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0900

llcv (2.0.5) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Follow the Windows LLCV 2.0.5 update.
  * Customizable keyboard shortcuts (Settings, Guide & logs). All eight
    viewer shortcuts, including Esc, accept a single key or a Ctrl/Alt/Shift
    combination. Duplicate, empty, Super and reserved combinations are
    rejected, and Reset defaults restores the original keys.
  * Keys are matched by scancode, so they work with any input method.
  * Help, menu bar, overlays and settings text show the assigned keys.

 -- Meohong <busimh001@gmail.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0900

llcv (2.0.4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Follow the Windows LLCV 2.0.3 and 2.0.4 updates.
  * Optional 40 fps capture (Video, off by default). It requests 40 fps from
    the driver even when the rate is not in the detected list, confirms the
    rate the driver reports on Start, and shows an error instead of falling
    back to another rate.
  * "Prevent sleep during playback" (App, on by default). Video keeps the
    display and system awake; audio-only lets the display turn off and only
    blocks automatic suspend through the desktop portal. The request is
    released when playback stops or the capture device disconnects. The
    screen saver is no longer blocked on the settings screen.
  * A failed settings save keeps the previous settings file, removes the
    temporary file and shows a notice.
  * The APT source lists only the package architecture, so systems with
    i386 multiarch (for example for Steam) no longer show "doesn't support
    architecture 'i386'" on apt update.

 -- Meohong <busimh001@gmail.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900

llcv (2.0.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * First Linux release, rewritten from the Windows LLCV 2.0.2 design.
  * V4L2 memory-mapped capture with latest-frame-first delivery and
    automatic reconnection.
  * OpenGL 3.3 presentation for NV12, YUY2, MJPEG (libjpeg-turbo) and BGR24.
  * SDL3 audio on PipeWire with the PCM queue target and clock-drift
    correction from the Windows build.
  * Dear ImGui settings screen, diagnostics and audio overlays with
    Korean and English text.
  * P010 (HDR10) capture, HDR10 passthrough through wp_color_management_v1
    on Wayland with a 10-bit framebuffer, and HDR to SDR tone mapping
    (the Windows screenshot curve) on SDR displays and X11.
  * Bundled Dear ImGui 1.92.2b so Debian 13, Ubuntu and Arch build the
    same code.
  * Ubuntu 24.04 support: pinned SDL3 3.4.18 linked statically through the
    pkg.llcv.bundled-sdl3 build profile, and a bundled color-management
    protocol file for older wayland-protocols.
  * The app states when HDR input or output is not supported, and why.
  * Alt shows a menu bar with the viewer commands.
  * NVIDIA VSR, WASAPI Exclusive and ASIO are not available on Linux.

 -- Meohong <busimh001@gmail.com>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900
